# GridWindow FlexPay environment template.
# Copy to .env.local (git-ignored) and replace every placeholder. Never commit real values.
# All payments are PayPal SANDBOX only; any PAYPAL_ENV other than "sandbox" stops startup.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# A. MOCK mode (default). No PayPal, Gemini or database credentials needed. Judges start here.
#    Embedded PostgreSQL (PGlite) stores data under GW_DATA_DIR.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
PAYMENT_MODE=mock
PAYPAL_ENV=sandbox
APP_BASE_URL=http://localhost:3000
# 32+ characters. Required in production; generate your own, e.g. `openssl rand -hex 32`.
SESSION_SECRET=replace-me-with-a-random-string-of-32-or-more-characters
# 12+ characters, or the operator console is disabled.
OPERATOR_PASSPHRASE=replace-me-operator-passphrase
# MOCK mode only, only without DATABASE_URL: shows "Seed background drivers" and "Reset demo data".
# DEMO_TOOLS=true
# Where the embedded database lives (default .data/pglite).
# GW_DATA_DIR=.data/pglite

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# B. PayPal SANDBOX mode. Needs your own sandbox REST app, a sandbox business (merchant) account
#    and a separate sandbox personal (buyer) account. Uncomment and fill in.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# PAYMENT_MODE=paypal_sandbox
# PAYPAL_ENV=sandbox
# PAYPAL_CLIENT_ID=replace-me
# PAYPAL_CLIENT_SECRET=replace-me
# Account ID of the sandbox business account that owns the REST app (10-20 upper-case letters/digits).
# Every approved order must name it as payee, or the app refuses to authorize.
# PAYPAL_EXPECTED_MERCHANT_ID=REPLACEME12345

# Webhooks (optional): needs a public HTTPS origin, e.g. a tunnel. Register
# https://<host>/api/webhooks/paypal in the sandbox app with the seven events listed in
# docs/PAYPAL_CERTIFICATION.md, then set the webhook ID PayPal shows. Without it every webhook is rejected.
# APP_BASE_URL=https://your-public-host.example
# PAYPAL_WEBHOOK_ID=replace-me
# Set to true ONLY behind a trusted proxy or tunnel (rate limiting then uses the last X-Forwarded-For hop).
# TRUST_PROXY=true
# Read-only readiness check (exits non-zero until the settings above are valid):
#   npm run payment:preflight -- --night-a YYYY-MM-DD --night-b YYYY-MM-DD

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# C. AI assistant (optional). Without a key, or on any provider failure, a labeled deterministic
#    parser/explainer runs. The model has no tools and cannot set prices or touch payments.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# AI_PROVIDER=gemini
# GEMINI_API_KEY=replace-me
# GEMINI_MODEL=gemini-3.6-flash
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=replace-me
# AI_MODEL=replace-with-an-anthropic-model-id

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# D. Hosted PostgreSQL (optional, e.g. Neon). Otherwise the embedded database is used.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# DATABASE_URL=postgres://user:password@host/dbname?sslmode=verify-full
# Optional direct (non-pooled) URL used only to run migrations.
# MIGRATION_DATABASE_URL=postgres://user:password@host/dbname?sslmode=verify-full

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# E. Test runners only. Do not set these in a real environment.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# GW_ISOLATED_DB=true       # makes startup refuse any hosted database, model key or non-mock payments
# TEST_DATABASE_URL=...     # throwaway LOCAL PostgreSQL for tests/integration/postgres.test.ts
# NEXT_DIST_DIR=.next       # build output directory (lets a verification build avoid a running server)
